	<key>readme</key>
	<string># 🎩 Alfred Dashlane

✨ *Search your Dashlane vault from Alfred* ✨

## ✅ Prerequisites

* macOS, Alfred 5 with the [Powerpack](https://www.alfredapp.com/powerpack/).
* A [Dashlane](https://www.dashlane.com) account with a master password (SSO / passwordless accounts are not supported).
* **Python 3.9** or above (`python3 --version`).

No Dashlane CLI needed: the workflow talks to Dashlane directly.

## 🧰 Setup

1. Fill `👤 Login` with your Dashlane email.
2. Type `pdash`. The first time, press ⏎ on **Install the crypto engine**: it installs the hash-pinned `cryptography` package (Argon2 + AES) in the workflow data folder.
3. Press ⏎ on **Login to Dashlane**: a Dashlane page opens in your browser. Paste the token it shows, then the 6-digit code (email or authenticator app), then your master password in the secure macOS dialog.

## 🧙‍♂️ Usage

* `pdash`: passwords. `odash`: OTP codes.
* ⏎ copy password (or OTP) · ⌘⏎ copy login · ⌥⏎ open URL · ⇧⏎ type login ⇥ password in the frontmost app · ⌃⏎ copy OTP.
* Copied secrets are marked transient (kept out of clipboard history) and erased after the delay you choose.

## 🔐 Security

* Master password typed only in a native hidden dialog, never through Alfred's bar, argv or env variables.
* Login verified with OPAQUE (the master password never leaves your Mac), pinned Dashlane server key.
* Local vault encrypted with AES-256-GCM. Its key is wrapped with Argon2id(master password) and only sits in your login keychain while unlocked. Auto-lock after inactivity.
* Nothing in clear on disk: no plaintext cache.

Full documentation on [GitHub](https://github.com/BenjaminOddou/alfred-dashlane).

© Benjamin Oddou
